[2026-09-07T00:44Z] STAGED-SET SCAN, run 1 — 63 FAIL / 70 PASS, over-fired
  command: npx tsx scripts/adr029-nonauthorial-scan.mts --target=ep-tiny-hat-atdgpisx --mode=scan
  Reading the findings (ADR-029: every hit is a claim to be read) showed the author-aware
  rules drowning in three false-positive classes: histories/biographies whose SUBJECT is
  another work ("The Life of William Gardiner" is Foxe's own chapter; schaff-hcc chapters),
  citations mid-body (". by R. Menzies", "Lightfoot's Commentary" in thayers), and all-caps
  poem/chapter titles ("SODOM'S DOOM", "ZION'S APPEAL", "NEW-YEAR'S GIFT"). Plus a
  chain-reference work tripping the price-list body rule on "--SEE Topic" lines.
  Detector rework (still DETECTOR_VERSION 2.0.0, same shapes, sharper bounds):
    - author-aware rules read the heading + body's first 120 chars only (title region);
    - a body match is STRONG only with the print-boundary signature (a rule line
      ————/____/---- within 160 chars), else WEAK; heading matches are WEAK (a heading
      naming another work usually declares the section's subject);
    - bylines require ≥2 name tokens (kills ". By Adam", ". By Inheritance");
    - all-caps possessive requires a work-type noun (kills "SODOM'S DOOM", keeps
      "HAYDN'S DICTIONARY"); "--" leader needs 4 hyphens (kills "--SEE" chain refs);
    - abstract-noun exclusions extended ("One's Life", "Life of Thought" — real Origen
      chapter headings that fired in run 1 of the labelled set).

